What are Spin Finishes?
Spin finishes are liquid chemical agents applied to synthetic fibers such as polyester, nylon and polypropylene during or immediately after extrusion. They function simultaneously as lubricants and anti‑static agents, lowering friction and preventing static buildup. By doing so, they ensure smooth processing into yarns and fabrics, reduce filament breakage, and support ultra‑high‑speed extrusion – a critical requirement for modern textile and technical‑fiber production.
